From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:19:14 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] webapi: mock native WebGL2 and shader precision queries

Expose separate native WebGLRenderingContext and WebGL2RenderingContext
interfaces from the existing WebGL module, without JS prototype inheritance.
Share the query implementation while selecting WebGL 1/2 and GLSL ES 1/3
version strings. Preserve the base MacBook Neo Apple A18 Pro / ANGLE Metal
identity, debug-extension gating, dimensions and clear-on-read error state.

Implement getShaderPrecisionFormat for both shader stages and all six
LOW/MEDIUM/HIGH FLOAT/INT enums. Use a deterministic synthetic profile:
low/medium float 15/15/10, high float 127/127/23, and integer 31/30/0.
These are chosen mock capabilities, not measurements from an A18 Pro Mac.
Invalid enums return null and latch INVALID_ENUM without clearing pending
errors on successful queries.

Return fresh WebGLShaderPrecisionFormat objects with readonly native
accessors and GC finalizer/ref-count hooks, so discarded query results and
their JS properties can be collected. Keep native receiver checks, method
arity and illegal constructors through the existing bridge.

Route and cache webgl2 independently in HTMLCanvasElement and OffscreenCanvas,
including worker realms, while preserving 2D/WebGL1/WebGL2 mutual exclusion
and existing canvas-export fallbacks. Add no unit tests and leave the
benchmark unchanged. Validate with existing upstream tests, the benchmark,
and ignored page/iframe/dedicated/shared/service worker and GC diagnostics.

This remains a query-only mock: shader compilation, graphics resources,
drawing and the separate WebGL/SVG functional assertion are not implemented.

References:
https://registry.khronos.org/webgl/specs/latest/1.0/
https://registry.khronos.org/webgl/specs/latest/2.0/
https://www.apple.com/macbook-neo/specs/
